Subject: [PATCH 07909/11362] [outer-loop] CORRIGENDUM: arm E was never
 measuring the reference -- it is unseeded AND livelocked. 'Reference
 underperforms' RETRACTED

The shim investigation answered the question and overturned my own reporting. Original numbers
preserved; the interpretations below are withdrawn.

CODE FIDELITY IS NOT THE PROBLEM: the clone is pristine (real reference, HEAD c2d9831, clean tree),
the shim subclasses the real HeuristicAgent, and both arms score levels through the SAME
_levels_completed function. Two other defects make arm E uninterpretable.

DEFECT 1 -- ARM E IS UNSEEDED. HeuristicAgent.__init__ does
  seed = int(time.time()*1000000) + hash(self.game_id)%1000000; random.seed(seed)
(agents/heuristic_agent.py:68-69) AFTER the harness seeds, clobbering it. Arm E's nine cells are
nine UNSEEDED draws: [5,5,6,6,6,7,7,8,10], sd 1.581 vs B2's 0.726. Its 4 reproduction checks were
Bernoulli re-draws, not determinism tests -- which fully explains the bp35 1->0 'failure'.

DEFECT 2 -- THE REFERENCE LIVELOCKS ON OUR RENDER. Its state hash blanks a 64-px status-bar row
that carries load-bearing state here, so distinct states alias, the graph records contradictory
successors, trips its own assert, and the recovery path re-issues without advancing. 72-97% of
choose_action calls raise. Causal proof: DELETING its frontier search takes lf52 0/6 -> 6/6 and
su15 0/6 -> 6/6. Over 62 runs: search-on 6/31 wins (exception fraction 0.771), search-off 19/31.

MISSING INSTRUMENT: all 225 arm-E rows carry states_expanded=None (A: 0/75 None, B2: 0/225 None).
Nothing in 975 cells could reveal a 72-97%-crashed control.

RETRACTED: (a) 'arm E scored 6.67, BELOW baseline 7.00' as a finding -- t(8) = -0.632 is PARITY;
(b) that the reference underperforms or is a weak yardstick -- NEITHER is supported, no run measured
the method rather than the crash (its published result is private levels, its own runner,
MAX_ACTIONS=1e6; our 2000 is 2.2%); (c) the 5-game complementary list -- an any-seed union
contradicting the artifact's own per-seed basis: ar25/cn04/ls20/tn36 are 1/9 noise, only r11l (9/9)
is real, and it wins 3/3 with the reference's search DELETED, so it comes from candidate sampling
not frontier discipline; (d) caveats[0] is factually INVERTED -- measured A/E env-interaction ratio
0.615/0.998/0.037/0.105, i.e. E does 1.0-27x MORE, not 4.2-4.4x less; (e) reproduction '29/30' is
26 determinism checks + 4 coin flips.

THE FLAG FLIP IS UNAFFECTED. A/B2/B2_nofix share the live explorer and a private
random.Random(frontier_discipline_seed), never the global RNG the reference clobbers. B2 mean 10.556
vs A 7.000, 8/9 per-seed dominance, B2-vs-B2_nofix 8/9 vs 3/9 -- all stand. The flip never rested
on arm E.

